-> Reference: constraint operators — =, <, >, ≤, ≥, ≠. Each narrows a
-> variable's domain; `=` narrows it all the way to one value in a
-> single step. A comparison against an unresolved variable is decided
-> from its domain when the domain settles it either way (see `b`, `e`).
a = 5
assert a = 5

b > 10
b < 20
assert b > 5

c ∈ Z
c > 0
c < 4
loop c get whole_numbers { yield c }
assert whole_numbers = [1, 2, 3]

d ≠ 5
d = 6
assert d = 6

e ≥ 3
e ≤ 10
assert e ≥ 3
